cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Laguna Genealogies: A Digital Edition of Parsons 1923"
message: >-
  If you use this edition, please cite both it and the 1923 publication it
  transcribes (see references).
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Heger-Vlahovic
    given-names: Elizabeth
abstract: >-
  A verified digital transcription of the genealogical plates published with
  Elsie Clews Parsons's "Laguna Genealogies" (1923). Table 1, "Genealogy I",
  records 104 individuals across five generations, with 27 marriages and 80
  parent-child links. Table 4, "Genealogy IV", records 73 individuals across
  four generations, with 14 marriages and 58 parent-child links. Both are
  transcribed character by character including Americanist phonetic diacritics,
  and encoded as a normalised persons/unions/children schema. Clan descent is
  matrilineal, which provides an independent structural check on every bracket
  reading.
keywords:
  - Laguna Pueblo
  - genealogy
  - Elsie Clews Parsons
  - Keresan
  - digital edition
  - Southwest anthropology
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/PuebloGenealogy/pueblogenealogy.github.io"
url: "https://pueblogenealogy.github.io/"
